{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/metering/pricing.py","line":282,"code_snippet":"def _long_context_fields(block):  # reads threshold_tokens, input_multiplier, output_multiplier — never `verified`","reasoning_trace":"The catalog marks the tier `verified: false` (model-config.yaml:406) yet _long_context_fields never reads the flag. Provider pricing page fetched 2026-10-22: 4.6+ models except Haiku 5.5 have the full 1M window at standard pricing. Repro R6: block with verified False returns a live tier.","finding":"Long-context premium billed from an unverified reference tier; if the published rule applies, >200K requests are over-reported 2x/1.5x and the budget enforcer trips early","critique":"The PR adds a verification flag and then ignores it.","remediation":"Gate the tier on verified: true or drop it until confirmed on an invoice; document source and date.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-682"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"concurrency","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/routing/ceiling.py","line":279,"code_snippet":"data = load_observed(path)\n... data.setdefault(\"entries\", []).append(row)\n... os.replace(tmp, path)","reasoning_trace":"record_observed is load -> append -> mkstemp + os.replace with no lock; parallel cheval processes (two dissent voices, Flatline voices) race and lose rows. Repo ledgers use flock.","finding":"Lockless read-modify-write on the observed-bound store loses concurrent observations","critique":"The bound tightens on the second verdict, not the first.","remediation":"fcntl.flock on a sidecar lock file (O_NOFOLLOW) around load + write.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-362"]}
{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"resource_limits","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/flatline-orchestrator.sh","line":1030,"code_snippet":"per_call_max_tokens=\"$(flatline_voice_max_tokens \"$model_override\")\"\n...\nargs+=(--max-tokens \"$per_call_max_tokens\")","reasoning_trace":"Every Anthropic voice now gets an explicit 64000; an explicit value bypasses default_max_tokens' transport awareness (16K non-streaming, 4096 legacy wire). Worst-case output spend per voice call x4. cycle-124-dispatch-budgets.bats:8 header contradicts the tests below it.","finding":"Explicit 64K --max-tokens on every Anthropic Flatline voice bypasses cheval's transport-aware default and raises worst-case spend 4x","critique":"cheval's own default is already min(64K|16K, max_output_tokens).","remediation":"Pass no --max-tokens for Anthropic entries whose catalog value exceeds the cap, or make the cap transport-aware; refresh the bats header.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-770"]}
{"id":"ARCH-003","category":"architecture","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":2297,"code_snippet":"except RateLimitError as _e:\n    if _ceiling_unverified:\n        return _calibration_needed_exit(... error_class=\"RATE_LIMIT_UNVERIFIED\" ...)","reasoning_trace":"RateLimitError carries no RPM-vs-token-rate discriminator; any 429 above the probed bound ends the run and writes a store row. The PR's own test asserts this (design decision). Newer tree adds token_limited and a test that an RPM 429 walks. Dissent DISS-C-003a.","finding":"Any 429 while unverified overrides the declared chain and writes a calibration row with no token-limit discriminator","critique":"A requests-per-minute throttle already backed off by the transport should walk.","remediation":"Take the non-walk path only when the 429 body names a token-rate limit.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-754"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"ssrf_hardening","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/base.py","line":342,"code_snippet":"with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=connect_timeout + read_timeout) as resp:\n    raw = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\")","reasoning_trace":"New http_get on the urllib path follows redirects forwarding x-api-key, accepts any scheme, reads unbounded. Same lineage as http_post; health_check now sends the live key to GET {endpoint}/models on every status run. Endpoint is operator config. Dissent DISS-C-005.","finding":"http_get follows redirects with the API key, accepts any scheme, reads an unbounded body","critique":"Hardening gap, not a new exploit.","remediation":"Disable redirects, enforce https, cap the read.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-918","CWE-200"]}
{"id":"CQ-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/metering/pricing.py","line":290,"code_snippet":"def _mult(value):\n    m = float(value) ... return m if m > 0 else 1.0","reasoning_trace":".inf is valid YAML; int(cost * inf) raises OverflowError inside create_ledger_entry after the billed call. Repro R6b reproduced the OverflowError. Dissent DISS-C-004.","finding":"Multiplier accepts inf/huge values; ledger write crashes after the call (unmetered spend) or inflates cost","critique":"'Malformed means no premium' promise not kept.","remediation":"Reject non-finite values; bound 0 < m <= 10.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1284"]}
{"id":"DO-001","category":"devops","criterion":"file_permissions","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/tools/ceiling-probe-live.py","line":173,"code_snippet":"fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=\".model-config.\", suffix=\".tmp\", dir=...)\nwith os.fdopen(fd, \"w\") as fh: fh.write(new)\nos.replace(tmp, path)","reasoning_trace":"mkstemp creates 0600; os.replace makes the System-Zone catalog 0600 after one run; no try/except unlink (ceiling.py:300-305 does it right); _PRICE_IN at :42 is a literal price map duplicating the catalog.","finding":"--write-catalog leaves the catalog 0600, can leak a temp file on error, and budgets from a literal price map","critique":"Contradicts the sprint's own 'derive from the catalog' principle.","remediation":"Preserve the original mode before replace; cleanup on exception; read input_per_mtok from the catalog.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-732","CWE-459"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"injection","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/loa-status.sh","line":806,"code_snippet":"eff=$(yq eval -r \".providers.anthropic.models.\\\"$model\\\".effective_input_ceiling // \\\"\\\"\" \"$cfg\")","reasoning_trace":"$model comes from the catalog's aliases.opus (trusted System Zone) and is interpolated into a yq path; jq side uses --arg correctly. Observations of 0 reach min and print 'observed -1'.","finding":"Alias target interpolated into a yq expression; zero observations render as -1","critique":"Low because the source is a repo-tracked config file.","remediation":"Use yq env()/--arg; filter observed_input_tokens > 0.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-94"]}
{"id":"CQ-007","category":"code_quality","criterion":"logging","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/anthropic_adapter.py","line":245,"code_snippet":"logger.log(_level, \"temperature %s dropped for %s ...\", temperature, request.model)","reasoning_trace":"Under LOA_CHEVAL_LEGACY_WIRE wire_temperature(None) returns 0.7 (base.py:177) and the old != 0.7 guard is gone, so every call to a temperature_supported:false entry logs a drop nobody requested.","finding":"Legacy-wire path logs 'temperature 0.7 dropped' on every thinking-model call","critique":"Noise that hides a real caller-supplied drop.","remediation":"Log only when request.temperature is not None.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-779"]}
